
Input String Manipulation in Python
String manipulation is the process of performing different operations on a string. Python provides many built-in functions and methods to manipulate strings easily.
1. Taking String Input
The input() function is used to take a string from the user.
name = input("Enter your name: ")
print(name)
2. Finding String Length
The len() function is used to find the number of characters in a string.
s = input("Enter a string: ")
print(len(s))
3. Converting to Uppercase
The upper() method converts all letters into uppercase.
s = input("Enter a string: ")
print(s.upper())
4. Converting to Lowercase
The lower() method converts all letters into lowercase.
s = input("Enter a string: ")
print(s.lower())
5. String Slicing
Slicing is used to access a part of a string.
s = input("Enter a string: ")
print(s[0:5])
6. Reversing a String
A string can be reversed using slicing.
s = input("Enter a string: ")
print(s[::-1])
7. Replacing Characters
The replace() method is used to replace a character or word.
s = input("Enter a string: ")
print(s.replace("a", "b"))
8. Splitting a String
The split() method divides a string into multiple parts.
s = input("Enter your full name: ")
print(s.split())
9. Finding a Character
The find() method is used to find the position of a character or substring.
s = input("Enter a string: ")
print(s.find("a"))
10. Removing Extra Spaces
The strip() method removes unnecessary spaces from the beginning and end of a string.
s = input("Enter a string: ")
print(s.strip())
Conclusion
Python provides several built-in functions and methods such as len(), upper(), lower(), replace(), split(), find(), and strip() for easy and efficient string manipulation.
